{
  "about": [
    "One entry per shetach. territory lists what it covers: a state or province code (US-TX, CA-ON); the part of a state east and/or west of a longitude ({ \"state\": \"US-PA\", \"westOf\": -78.13 }); counties by 5-digit FIPS ({ \"counties\": [...] }); towns ({ \"state\": \"US-MA\", \"towns\": [...] }); or census tracts ({ \"state\": \"US-MA\", \"tracts\": [...] }).",
    "Where claims overlap, the more specific one wins: tracts, then towns, then counties, then longitude lines, then whole states. Anything no shetach claims is left blank.",
    "short: the label used where the name doesn't fit; by default the state and province abbreviations joined (KS-MO). capital: the chabad.org center id of the shetach's headquarters (the number in its chabad.org link), or lat and lon; \"world\": true marks 770. lastName is optional; it defaults to the last word of headShliach. notShown: areas left off the map entirely."
  ],
